# Rename this file to `.gitignore` after copying the template.
#
# What git covers here: the pre-run and post-run commits in each TASK.md capture
# task-definition edits only (TASK.md, TASK_REFERENCE.md, CONFIG.md, the generate_*.py
# scripts). Everything ignored below is personal runtime state. It stays out of git on
# purpose, so a git snapshot does NOT hold it. Back it up yourself — see
# bootstrap/SETUP.md, "Git snapshots and backup".

# System / runtime status
SYSTEM_STATUS.md

# Generated output directories (contain personal data — do not commit)
# (Actions/ also covers Actions/WeekPlans/)
Actions/
Profile/
Knowledge/

# Timestamp files
**/LAST_RUN.txt

# Run / scan / maintenance logs
**/RUN_LOG.md
**/RUN_LOG_ARCHIVE.md
**/SCAN_LOG.md
**/MAINTENANCE_LOG.md

# Task self-improvement and issue tracking (generated by runs)
**/IMPROVEMENTS*.md
**/ISSUES_LOG.md
**/LESSONS.md
**/SIGNAL_LOG.md
**/MAINTENANCE_PLAN.md

# JSON state files
**/pending_actions.json
**/pending_actions.json.bak
**/resolved_archive.json
**/urgent_data.json

# Credentials
credentials.json
token.json
*.oauth
.env
.env.*

# Bootstrap stubs — explicitly included despite global ignore rules above
!bootstrap/**

# Local operations records and credentials (git hygiene, not access control).
OPERATIONS.local.md
!.env.example
